PBE noncollinear Fe2 regression for gga_grad=2, including forces and stress.

Derived from 038_PW_NC with different initial spin directions on the two atoms,
explicit PBE/gga_grad settings, and scf_thr=1e-10.
The initial moments point in different directions and decay towards zero during
SCF. This case exercises the noncollinear path including its weak-moment limit;
it is not a regression for a stable magnetic ground state.
The pseudopotential is reused from tests/PP_ORB; no numerical orbitals are needed.

From tests/01_PW, run:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /path/to/abacus -n 4 -r '^038_PW_NC_GGA_GRAD2$'

result.ref is generated with one MPI rank using the same command with -n 1 -g.
The reference covers energy per atom, the force summary, and the stress summary.
Default Autotest tolerances apply; no case-specific threshold overrides are used.
This SCF regression complements the XC module's density/stress derivative tests.
